WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:10.090
In case all of you in America missed the turkeys
running down the street for dear life, tomorrow

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:11.540
is Thanksgiving.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.710
Without even a close second, Thanksgiving
is my favorite holiday of the year.

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:22.000
I find focusing on the 3 F's: Family, friends
and food, usually brings out the best in just

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.369
about everyone.

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:27.660
Between the triptophan from the Turkey, your
booze of choice and football in the background,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:33.190
all of us, at least in my experience, are
just a little better on this day we've set

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:37.220
aside to give thanks for all the goodness
in our lives.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.159
Thanksgiving is the ultimate reminder of what
it means to be American.

00:00:41.159 --> 00:00:45.700
While most of us have the usual staples of
turkey, mashed potatoes, stuffing and cranberry

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:50.680
sauces around the table, we also bring in
traditions from our own cultures, ethnicities

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.330
and nationalities.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:58.510
This blending of flavors, languages and customs
from all over the world is what makes Thanksgiving

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:03.379
uniquely American, no offense to Canadian
Thanksgiving.

00:01:03.379 --> 00:01:08.290
The melting pot we've created here has given
more freedom to more people from more walks

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:12.120
of life than any other country in the history
of the world.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.610
Today people still yearn to come to America
to take part in our freedom and pretty much

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:21.750
nobody wants to leave no matter how often
celebrities say they will.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.850
This doesn't mean we are perfect, or anywhere
close to it, but it does mean that our tradition

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:33.130
of freedom, rooted in the pursuit of life,
liberty and happiness is a pretty good starting

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:37.840
point for how to build a truly liberal and
tolerant society.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:43.250
While politics will undoubtedly be discussed
around the Thanksgiving table this year, I'm

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:48.360
going to do my best to try to veer the conversation
always to what brings us together, rather

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.570
than what rips us apart.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:53.320
Maybe your uncle is pro-life and you're pro-choice.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.750
Maybe your sister voted for Hillary, but you
voted for Trump.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:00.810
Maybe you want low taxes, and your dad wants
to redistribute wealth.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:07.300
Whatever those differences are, they are actually
the very reason that this country is so great.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:11.420
We all get to have our own opinion and fight
for what we believe.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:15.530
But beyond just the ability to be tolerant
of people who are different from us, it's

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:21.450
more important that we can still learn from,
live with, and even love people who think

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:22.590
differently from us.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:27.120
I hope you have a wonderful day tomorrow,
filled with the those three F's I mentioned

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.959
earlier -- friends, family and food, and maybe
even one more F if you get lucky.

00:02:31.959 --> 00:02:37.510
Either way, let's give thanks tomorrow for
all the goodness we have, but often forget

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.060
to even acknowledge.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:41.030
Happy Thanksgiving to you and all your loved
ones...

